# RaktSetu environment variables
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in values from your Supabase project.
# These are PUBLIC (anon) keys — safe to expose in the browser, protected by RLS.
# NEVER put the service-role key here or in any file used by client code.
#
# ── Netlify ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# A deployed site reads these from the Netlify UI, NOT from a file:
#   Site configuration → Environment variables → add each name below → redeploy.
# The two NEXT_PUBLIC_ values are inlined into the browser bundle at BUILD
# time, so they must be present when Netlify runs `npm run build` — setting
# them only at runtime is not sufficient.
#
# 1. NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL        https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
#      Supabase → Project Settings → Data API (or the project URL)
# 2. NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY   the project's public "anon" key
#      Supabase → Project Settings → API Keys → "anon" / "publishable"
# 3. CRON_SECRET                     any long random string you choose
#      Shared secret for /api/cron/tick. The endpoint returns 503 and runs
#      nothing without it, so it is safe to omit if you do not use an external
#      scheduler. Generate one with:  openssl rand -hex 32
#
# In Supabase → Authentication → URL Configuration, also add:
#   - Site URL:       https://<your-site>.netlify.app
#   - Redirect URLs:  https://<your-site>.netlify.app/auth/callback
#     (email-confirmation and password-reset links return to /auth/callback)
#
# ── Local development ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy this file to .env.local and fill in the same two NEXT_PUBLIC_ values,
# then restart `npm run dev`.

NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-key
# CRON_SECRET=
